"lifesaver.instructions.body" = "Lifesaver cards are small transparent cards (or printed on white paper) with two identical ring or circle patterns side by side. You can obtain them from a vision therapist or print a standard lifesaver card template.\n\nHold the card at arm\U2019s length. Slowly allow your eyes to relax and diverge \U2014 as if looking through the card at something far away. A third ring should appear to float in the center between the two printed rings. This is the fused image.\n\nOnce you see the third ring, try to bring it into clear focus and hold it for 5\U201310 seconds. Gradually move the card closer as you improve. Stop immediately if you feel eye strain, headache, or discomfort.";
